89,"pass_rate":0.6842,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6087,"def_epa_per_play":-0.287},{"week":5,"opponent":"BUF","home":true,"pf":34.0,"pa":37.0,"off_snaps":79,"epa_per_play":0.2306,"pass_rate":0.7089,"pass_rate_neutral":0.7,"def_epa_per_play":0.2914},{"week":6,"opponent":"ARI","home":true,"pf":16.0,"pa":18.0,"off_snaps":57,"epa_per_play":-0.1551,"pass_rate":0.6491,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6087,"def_epa_per_play":-0.0206},{"week":7,"opponent":"LV","home":false,"pf":35.0,"pa":21.0,"off_snaps":65,"epa_per_play":0.174,"pass_rate":0.4615,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6522,"def_epa_per_play":-0.1626}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2022,"team":"MIN","distance":0.6415,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kevin O'Connell"},{"season":2023,"team":"MIN","distance":0.7311,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kevin O'Connell"},{"season":2024,"team":"HOU","distance":0.7789,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Bobby Slowik"},{"season":2023,"team":"DAL","distance":0.8203,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Mike McCarthy"},{"season":2025,"team":"JAX","distance":0.8212,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Liam Coen"}],"defense":[{"season":2024,"team":"MIA","distance":0.1032,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"CIN","distance":0.2087,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"},{"season":2023,"team":"KC","distance":0.2241,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Steve Spagnuolo"},{"season":2025,"team":"NE","distance":0.2327,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"IND","distance":0.2568,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Rams are 3-4 through week 7 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 170 to 159. Both sides of the ball have been strong, with the offense 10th in EPA per play and the defense 5th in EPA allowed. What sets them apart is the 2nd highest early-down pass rate in the league.","offense":"The Rams offense has been well above average by EPA per play so far. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the lowest RPO rate in the league. Matthew Stafford has run the passing game, with Puka Nacua leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Rams have one of the best defenses in the league this season, ranking 7th or better in three of the five main efficiency measures. Its strongest area has been EPA allowed per play, where it ranks 5th, and its weakest has been sack rate, where it ranks 28th. Byron Young has led the way with 4.5 sacks. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is an eight man box rate that ranks 14th highest in the league.","special":"The Rams have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 60% of field goals, which is the worst in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the secondary, about 24% of the money on the books. Their offensive line was among the oldest in the league.","players":"Matthew Stafford has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,989 yards. Puka Nacua has been the clear top target with 23% of the looks and 485 receiving yards. Kyren Williams has handled most of the work in the backfield with 56% of the carries. On defense, Byron Young leads the team with 4.5 sacks and Quentin Lake has picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"Sean McVay is calling the offense as head coach and Chris Shula is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2022 and 2023 Vikings, both under Kevin O'Connell. Their defense looks most like the 2024 Dolphins and the 2024 Bengals under Lou Anarumo.","trends":"The offense went from 2nd in EPA per play in 2025 to 10th so far this season, a big step back. The defense moved from 9th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 5th so far this season, a modest improvement. The biggest change in approach was fourth down go rate, which went from 58% to 33%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}